contracts — all are inline above. Reading them again wastes a turn and adds no information. Only use Read for files not present in project_context.\n9689\t    - Do NOT explore the filesystem. Do NOT run ls, find, tree, or similar commands.\n9690\t    - Do NOT modify files outside the Files to Create/Modify list unless a requirement explicitly demands it.\n9691\t    - Do NOT use bd or cupboard commands. Task tracking is handled externally.\n9692\t    - Do NOT invent interfaces, types, or patterns not described in the source code, Required Reading, or SRDs.\n9693\t    - Do NOT add features, refactoring, or improvements beyond what the requirements specify.\n9694\t    - Do NOT run any git commands. No git add, git commit, git init, git status, rm .git, or any other git operation. Git is managed externally by the orchestrator. Just write code and verify it compiles and passes tests.\n9695\t    - When building cmd/ binaries to verify compilation, use `go build -o bin/<name> ./cmd/<name>/` so outputs land in bin/ (which is git-ignored) rather than in the working directory.\n9696\t    - When a build or lint step fails, read ALL error and warning messages before making any changes. Fix every reported issue in a single edit pass, then run the build once to verify. Do not fix one issue, rebuild, fix the next — batch all fixes into one round.\n9697\t    - When modifying more than 3 locations in the same file, prefer the Write tool (full file replacement) over multiple Edit calls. Each Edit changes the file, invalidating old_string matches for subsequent Edits. Write avoids this by producing the complete file in one call.\n9698\t    - The test suite is the acceptance gate. Do not manually run binaries to compare output against reference implementations. Run `go test` and fix any failures. Manual comparison is only warranted when a test fails and the expected behavior is ambiguous.\n9699\t    - Complete all code changes before running `go build` or `go test`. Do not compile incrementally after each small edit. Mentally verify imports, types, and function signatures, then build once.\n9700\tdescription: |-\n9701\t    deliverable_type: code\n9702\t\n9703\t    required_reading:\n9704\t      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml (full SRD -- all requirements must have test coverage)\n9705\t      - cmd/truncate/main.go (implementation under test)\n9706\t      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness -- DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function)\n9707\t      - cmd/stat/stat_test.go (reference test file for a similar file-metadata utility)\n9708\t\n9709\t    files:\n9710\t      - path: cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go\n9711\t        action: create\n9712\t        note: Differential tests comparing Go truncate against gtruncate from Homebrew GNU coreutils\n9713\t\n9714\t    requirements:\n9715\t      - id: R1\n9716\t        text: Create TestDiff using testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") and exec.LookPath(\"gtruncate\") with t.Skip if reference binary not found\n9717\t      - id: R2\n9718\t        text: Write DiffTest cases covering all srd083 requirements R1.1 through R3.3 -- exact size, relative size (+/-), --reference, --no-create, multiple files, and error conditions\n9719\t      - id: R3\n9720\t        text: Verify exit code, stdout, and stderr match between Go and GNU binaries for each test case\n9721\t      - id: R4\n9722\t        text: Test edge cases including zero-byte truncation, nonexistent files with and without --no-create, and invalid --size values\n9723\t\n9724\t    design_decisions:\n9725\t      - id: D1\n9726\t        text: Use testutils.RunDiffTests for all differential test cases per project convention\n9727\t      - id: D2\n9728\t        text: Reference binary is gtruncate (Homebrew GNU coreutils with g-prefix)\n9729\t      - id: D3\n9730\t        text: Set LC_ALL=C in test environment per project convention\n9731\t      - id: D4\n9732\t        text: Create temp files and directories in t.TempDir() for test fixtures -- do not leave test artifacts\n9733\t\n9734\t    acceptance_criteria:\n9735\t      - id: AC1\n9736\t        text: \"go test ./cmd/truncate/ -count=1\" passes (or skips gracefully if gtruncate not found)\n9737\t      - id: AC2\n9738\t        text: Tests cover exact size, relative size (+/-), --reference, --no-create, multi-file processing, and error scenarios\n9739\t      - id: AC3\n9740\t        text: All test cases use the DiffTest/RunDiffTests pattern from pkg/testutils\n9741\t      - id: AC4\n9742\t        text: \"go vet ./cmd/truncate/\" passes with no warnings\n9743\tshared_protocols:\n9744\t    - name: Differential testing\n9745\t      description: |\n9746\t        Every cmd/ package verifies its implementation by running the Go binary and the\n9747\t        Homebrew GNU reference binary side by side and comparing stdout, stderr, and exit\n9748\t        code via pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests. Test cases are defined as []testutils.DiffTest\n9749\t        slices in <utility>_test.go files. The harness sets LC_ALL=C by default.\n9750\t      pattern: |\n9751\t        func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n9752\t            goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n9753\t            refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\")\n9754\t            if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n9755\t            tests := []testutils.DiffTest{ ... }\n9756\t            testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n9757\t        }\n9758\t    - name: Graceful skip on missing reference binary\n9759\t      description: |\n9760\t        All cmd/ test files call exec.LookPath for the Homebrew reference binary at the\n9761\t        start of TestDiff and call t.Skip if it is not found. This allows the test suite\n9762\t        to run on machines without Homebrew GNU binaries installed without reporting false\n9763\t        failures. The binary is never installed by the test itself.\n9764\t      pattern: |\n9765\t        refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"g<utility>\")\n9766\t        if err != nil { t.Skipf(\"reference binary g<utility> not in PATH: %v\", err) }\n9767\t    - name: SIGPIPE handling\n9768\t      description: |\n9769\t        All cmd/ utilities that write to stdout call pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at\n9770\t        the start of main. This ensures the process exits 0 when piped output is consumed\n9771\t        by a downstream consumer that closes its stdin (e.g., head, grep -q), matching GNU\n9772\t        coreutils behavior.\n9773\t      pattern: |\n9774\t        func main() {\n9775\t            sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n9776\t            ...\n9777\t        }\n9778\tpackage_contracts:\n9779\t    - srd_id: srd001-testutils\n9780\t      contract:\n9781\t        exports:\n9782\t            - name: DiffTest\n9783\t              signature: type DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }\n9784\t            - name: NormalizeFunc\n9785\t              signature: type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\n9786\t            - name: RunDiffTests\n9787\t              signature: func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n9788\t            - name: ComposeNormalizers\n9789\t              signature: func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc\n9790\t            - name: TimestampNormalizer\n9791\t              signature: var TimestampNormalizer NormalizeFunc\n9792\t        imports:\n9793\t            - testing\n9794\t            - os\n9795\t            - os/exec\n9796\t        import_constraints:\n9797\t            - Must not import any cmd/ package.\n9798\t            - Must not import any other pkg/ package.\n9799\t    - srd_id: srd002-sys\n9800\t      contract:\n9801\t        exports:\n9802\t            - name: FileInfo\n9803\t              signature: type FileInfo struct { Mode os.FileMode; Size int64; Nlink uint64; Uid uint32; Gid uint32; Rdev uint64; Dev uint64; Ino uint64; Blocks int64; Blksize int64; ModTime time.Time; AccessTime time.Time; ChangeTime time.Time; Info os.FileInfo }\n9804\t            - name: Stat\n9805\t              signature: func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\n9806\t            - name: Lstat\n9807\t              signature: func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\n9808\t            - name: TerminalWidth\n9809\t              signature: func TerminalWidth() (int, error)\n9810\t            - name: IsTerminal\n9811\t              signature: func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool\n9812\t            - name: InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n9813\t              signature: func InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n9814\t            - name: OnTerminalResize\n9815\t              signature: func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))\n9816\t        imports:\n9817\t            - os\n9818\t            - os/signal\n9819\t            - syscall\n9820\t            - time\n9821\t            - golang.org/x/sys/unix\n9822\t        import_constraints:\n9823\t            - Must not import any cmd/ package.\n9824\t            - Must not import any other pkg/ package.\n9825\t    - srd_id: srd003-format\n9826\t      contract:\n9827\t        exports:\n9828\t            - name: HumanSizeOpts\n9829\t              signature: type HumanSizeOpts struct { Binary bool }\n9830\t            - name: HumanSize\n9831\t              signature: func HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string\n9832\t            - name: FileTypeColor\n9833\t              signature: func FileTypeColor(mode os.FileMode) string\n9834\t            - name: Reset\n9835\t              signature: func Reset() string\n9836\t            - name: ColorEnabled\n9837\t              signature: func ColorEnabled(w io.Writer) bool\n9838\t            - name: SetColorEnabled\n9839\t              signature: func SetColorEnabled(enabled bool)\n9840\t            - name: ResetColorEnabled\n9841\t              signature: func ResetColorEnabled()\n9842\t            - name: PadRight\n984